1779.docs:
Rebuilds the UI from any thread, when background work has something to show.

Get one with [`BuildCx::ui_waker`](crate::BuildCx::ui_waker) and move it to
the thread. Send the result through a channel and call [`UiWaker::wake`]; the
next build runs on the UI thread and reads the channel. Between wakes the app
stays asleep, so there is nothing to poll.

```
use std::sync::mpsc::channel;
use ravenrs_widgets::{BuildCx, NodeId, View};

struct Pump;

impl View for Pump {
    fn build(&self, cx: &mut BuildCx<'_>) -> NodeId {
        let waker = cx.ui_waker();
        let (send, _receive) = channel();
        std::thread::spawn(move || {
            let _ = send.send(21 * 2);
            waker.wake();
        });
        cx.empty()
    }
}
```

The web build has no other threads to wake it from; there, change a
[`State`](ravenrs_reactive::State) as usual.

14351.docs:
A list that reorders by dragging a row, with a line showing where it will land, or with Alt
and the arrows, Home and End. The arrows alone move between rows, and each move is announced to
screen readers. The order belongs to the app, which applies what
[`on_reorder`](Self::on_reorder) tells it.

```
use ravenrs_reactive::State;
use ravenrs_widgets::{SortableList, Text, Ui};

let items = State::new(vec!["Warm", "Cool", "Matte"]);
let shown = items.get();
let moved = items.clone();
let list = SortableList::new(shown.len(), move |i| Text::new(shown[i]))
    .on_reorder(move |from, to| moved.update(|v| {
        let item = v.remove(from);
        v.insert(to, item);
    }));
let mut ui = Ui::new(list, ravenrs_style::Theme::raven_dark());
ui.update();
```

